    "label": "th:borneRegret",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "Consider a bandit problem with $K$ arms and independent rewards bounded in $[0,1]$, and denote by $a^*$ an optimal arm. Choosing $c=3$, the regret of the KL-UCB algorithm satisfies: \\[\\limsup_{n\\to\\infty} \\frac{\\E[R_n]}{\\log(n)} \\leq \\sum_{a:\\mu_a<\\mu_{a^*}} \\frac{\\mu_{a^*}-\\mu_a}{d(\\mu_a, \\mu_{a^*})}\\;.\\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "d is the Bernoulli KL, so d(mu_a, mu_star) = kl_i. Regret defined vs best expected arm, recorded as pseudo-regret. Corollary 3 (Bernoulli rewards: matches Lai-Robbins lower bound) is a special case, not recorded separately. The paper also claims (in prose, Section 4) the same limsup bound for exponential-family variants of KL-UCB with d = KL of the family; not a formal statement."
  },
